#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180602} :activity/id #uuid "e6fba530-9f3d-5ad2-a58a-2010478f12bf" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048392 :topic/id #uuid "9b9bc1e8-8910-5e7b-b200-0bc492f56034" :topic/math-academy-id 3719} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180602 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180768 :tutorial/content "Let's remind ourselves of the three rules for dividing with negative numbers:\n\n- A negative number divided by a positive number gives a negative number. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-)\\,÷\\,(+)\\,=\\,(-)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- A positive number divided by a negative number is also a negative number. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(+)\\,÷\\,(-)\\,=\\,(-)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- A negative number divided by a negative number is a positive number.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-)\\,÷\\,(-)\\,=\\,(+)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "19bbbf1e-a31e-54b1-92bb-a2fb71bf54b8" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8022 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "b2427cba-ac8b-55c2-95b7-2a0f2be0812b" :step/math-academy-id 53469 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180603}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180603 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180769 :tutorial/content "As an example, let's find the value of\n\n$$\n2.4 \\div (-4).\n$$\n\nDividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since \n\n$$\n2.4\\div 4=0.6,\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n2.4 \\div (-4) = -0.6.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "3c2ea5e2-fa57-573b-8e38-712b30958ca4" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8023 :tutorial/title "A Worked Example"} :step/id #uuid "c0f81736-6a5b-5d18-9f29-8ef5290d319e" :step/math-academy-id 53470 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180604}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180604 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179798 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179445 :question/id #uuid "4fc788a3-fcac-5de0-a92b-8e818ce41160" :question/math-academy-id